-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 version 0.2.0: worked households for the paths row IL-08 opened.
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE COMES FROM THE SOURCE AND THE ROWS' SOURCED FIGURES,
-- worked by hand in NOTES.md section 11 (and checked there with exact fractions
-- in a calculator that reads no L4), never from running this code. The figures
-- of il07-tests.l4, and:
--   s 45A/47 amounts 2026 .. 2,268 (s 45A(d)(1)); 116,400 and 164,400 (s 47(a)(1)
--                            (1), (2)); the average wage 165,228 a year, so a
--                            beneficiary member has 26,436.48 deposited (s 47(a)(7));
--                            each twelve times the Tax Authority's monthly figure
--                            ([booklet-2026] p. 9; row IL-08, its A3, A4)
--   s 45A rates ............ 25% life insurance; 35% pension and survivors'
--                            insurance; (d) 7% of qualifying income for work
--                            income, provisos 1.5% and 5%; (e)(2)(b)(2)(a) 7% of
--                            insured qualifying income (ITO lines 1715-1738)
--   s 40(b) tables ......... (1): 2 1/2 in the year of birth, 4 1/2 aged 1-2,
--                            3 1/2 aged 3, 2 1/2 aged 4-5, 2 aged 6-17, 1/2 at
--                            18; (1A): the same to 5, then 1; (1B) one more point
--                            and the (1A) table; (2) one more point (lines 1633-1640)
--   s 35 ................... from Amendment 262: 1/12 a month for months 1-12 of
--                            the period, 1/4 for 13-30, 1/6 for 31-42, 1/12 for
--                            43-54 (lines 1575-1578)
--   s 37 ................... one point; half of it in a separate calculation,
--                            s 66(c)(2) (lines 1600, 2463)
--   NII s 72 ............... paid from the month of birth if born by the 15th, else
--                            the next; to the month of the 18th birthday (line 854)
--   NII s 335 .............. the branches by status (lines 3611-3619)
--   NII Schedule A1 Part D . 70 years (840 months) for a woman born from May 1950;
--                            69 and 8 months (836) for one born September 1949 to
--                            April 1950 (lines 4452-4453)
--   Schedule J 2026, col. D  per branch, below / above the threshold: maternity
--                            0.10 / 0.87, accident injury 0.03 / 0.07,
--                            unemployment 0.02 / 0.21, disability 0.29 / 1.86,
--                            long-term care 0.03 / 0.14, senior citizens and
--                            survivors 0.57 / 1.52; printed totals 1.04 / 7.00
--                            (NII lines 4720-4730, row IL-04's temporary version)
--   SCHEDULE J, BY RULING .. Meng ruled on 2026-10-07 that column D is read at its
--                            printed totals, 1.04 / 7.00, by default, the items'
--                            reading kept as a fork (NOTES.md K14). Every
--                            deduction above 7,703 here is at the printed totals;
--                            the values first worked at the items' 4.67 are
--                            marked "CHANGED BY THE SCHEDULE J RULING" with the
--                            figure they replaced (NOTES.md section 11.13).
-- A failing assertion is a finding: no expected value here is ever edited to
-- match what the code computed.
-- VERSION 0.3.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-22): the rows' repairs of that day turn
-- eight of this module's refusals into answers or into a row's own words; each
-- is marked "CHANGED IN 0.3.0" with what it replaced, worked by hand from the
-- source before the run (NOTES.md section 12). Section 35's new last part holds
-- the tests of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 version 0.2.0 — worked households`

§§ `Builders`

GIVEN `the name` IS A STRING
      `is female` IS A BOOLEAN
      `born on`  IS A DATE
      `salary`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 earner`
`v2: an earner` `the name` `, female:` `is female` `, born` `born on` `, paid` `salary` MEANS
    `IL-07 earner` WITH
        `the earner's name`                                                              IS `the name`
        `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS `is female`
        `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS `born on`
        `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS `salary`
        `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
        `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
        `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
        `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS NOTHING
        `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE

GIVEN `her name` IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `IL-07 spouse`
`v2: a housewife named` `her name` MEANS
    `IL-07 spouse` WITH
        `the spouse's name`                                                              IS `her name`
        `the spouse is a woman`                                                          IS TRUE
        `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS 0
        `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS FALSE
        `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE

GIVEN `the other spouse`  IS AN `IL-07 spouse`
      `registered`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 couple`
`v2: married to` `the other spouse` `, registered:` `registered` `, claims:` `claims` `, s 37:` `s 37` MEANS
    `IL-07 couple` WITH
        `the earner's spouse`                                                            IS `the other spouse`
        `the earner is the registered spouse`                                            IS `registered`
        `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion` IS `claims`
        `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS `s 37`

GIVEN `the name` IS A STRING
      `born on`  IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `IL-07 child`
`v2: a child` `the name` `, born` `born on` MEANS
    `IL-07 child` WITH
        `the child's name`                                                               IS `the name`
        `the child's date of birth`                                                      IS `born on`
        `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the month`  IS A NUMBER
      `who earns`  IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the couple` IS A MAYBE `IL-07 couple`
      `the kids`   IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `health`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 household in a month`
`v2: in month` `the month` `of 2026, a household of` `who earns` `, married:` `the couple` `, with children` `the kids` `, health` `health` MEANS
    `IL-07 household in a month` WITH
        `the year of the month`                                                          IS 2026
        `the month of the year`                                                          IS `the month`
        `the earner`                                                                     IS `who earns`
        `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`                                         IS `the couple`
        `the children of the household`                                                  IS `the kids`
        `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month`    IS `health`

GIVEN `own`       IS A NUMBER
      `employer`  IS A NUMBER
      `insured`   IS A NUMBER
      `survivors` IS A NUMBER
      `life`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 the earner's pension contributions and insurance`
`v2: paying` `own` `a month, the employer` `employer` `, insured` `insured` `, survivors' insurance` `survivors` `, life insurance` `life` MEANS
    `IL-07 the earner's pension contributions and insurance` WITH
        `the earner's own contribution to a pension provident fund, each month`          IS `own`
        `the employer's deposits to a pension provident fund for the earner, each month` IS `employer`
        `the part of the monthly salary that is insured income`                          IS `insured`
        `paid in the tax year for survivors' pension insurance`                          IS `survivors`
        `paid in the tax year for insurance of the earner's or the spouse's life`        IS `life`

GIVEN p IS AN `IL-07 the earner's pension contributions and insurance`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 further facts of the household`
`v2: further facts, paying` p MEANS
    `IL-07 further facts of the household` WITH
        `the earner's pension contributions and insurance`         IS p
        `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`  IS NOTHING
        `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`                  IS NOTHING
        `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given` IS NOTHING
        `the single-parent family, if given`                       IS NOTHING

`v2: nothing paid` MEANS `v2: paying` 0 `a month, the employer` 0 `, insured` 0 `, survivors' insurance` 0 `, life insurance` 0

GIVEN `single`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `entries`  IS A LIST OF `IL-07 a child's other parent, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 further facts of the household`
`v2: a single parent, single-parent family:` `single` `, living apart:` `apart` `, other parents` `entries` MEANS
    `IL-07 further facts of the household` WITH
        `the earner's pension contributions and insurance`         IS `v2: nothing paid`
        `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`  IS NOTHING
        `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`                  IS NOTHING
        `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given` IS NOTHING
        `the single-parent family, if given`                       IS JUST (`IL-07 the single-parent family, for section 40(b)` WITH
            `the earner and the children are a single-parent family` IS `single`
            `the earner maintained the children in the tax year`     IS TRUE
            `the earner lives apart from the children's other parent` IS `apart`
            `the earner's share of the children's maintenance expenses` IS 1
            `each child's other parent`                              IS `entries`)

GIVEN `the child's name` IS A STRING
      `died`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unregistered`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 a child's other parent, for section 40(b)`
`v2: the other parent of` `the child's name` `, died:` `died` `, not registered:` `unregistered` MEANS
    `IL-07 a child's other parent, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `the name of the child`                                                          IS `the child's name`
        `the child's other parent died in or before the tax year`                                IS `died`
        `the child is registered in the population register without the details of one parent` IS `unregistered`
        `the child's other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                        IS TRUE
        `the child's other parent has credit points for the child under section 40(b)(1)`        IS FALSE

GIVEN im IS AN `IL-07 the earner's immigration`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 further facts of the household`
`v2: an immigrant,` im MEANS
    `IL-07 further facts of the household` WITH
        `the earner's pension contributions and insurance`         IS `v2: nothing paid`
        `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`  IS JUST im
        `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`                  IS NOTHING
        `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given` IS NOTHING
        `the single-parent family, if given`                       IS NOTHING

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `first`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 the earner's immigration`
`v2: immigrated under the Law of Return on` `the day` `, the first time:` `first` MEANS
    `IL-07 the earner's immigration` WITH
        `the ground of immigration`                                                      IS `IL-07: an immigrant's visa or certificate under the Law of Return`
        `the earner's Israeli citizenship was cancelled under section 10(d) of the Citizenship Law` IS FALSE
        `the day the earner became an immigrant`                                         IS `the day`
        `it was the first time the earner became an immigrant`                           IS `first`
        `the Minister's rules under section 35(e) reach the earner`                      IS FALSE

GIVEN s IS AN `IL-07 the statuses section 37 reads`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 further facts of the household`
`v2: with the statuses section 37 reads,` s MEANS
    `IL-07 further facts of the household` WITH
        `the earner's pension contributions and insurance`         IS `v2: nothing paid`
        `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`  IS NOTHING
        `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`                  IS JUST s
        `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given` IS NOTHING
        `the single-parent family, if given`                       IS NOTHING

GIVEN `spouse disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 the statuses section 37 reads`
`v2: maintenance proved, the spouse blind or disabled:` `spouse disabled` MEANS
    `IL-07 the statuses section 37 reads` WITH
        `the earner has reached retirement age`                                          IS FALSE
        `the earner's spouse has reached retirement age`                                          IS FALSE
        `the earner is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`                 IS FALSE
        `the earner's spouse is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`                 IS `spouse disabled`
        `the earner proved to the assessing officer that the spouse's maintenance was on the earner in the tax year` IS TRUE

GIVEN s IS AN `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 further facts of the household`
`v2: with the insurance statuses` s MEANS
    `IL-07 further facts of the household` WITH
        `the earner's pension contributions and insurance`         IS `v2: nothing paid`
        `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`  IS NOTHING
        `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`                  IS NOTHING
        `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given` IS JUST s
        `the single-parent family, if given`                       IS NOTHING

GIVEN `work injury only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `controlling`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335`
`v2: statuses, insured for work injury only:` `work injury only` `, a controlling shareholder:` `controlling` MEANS
    `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335` WITH
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 5, work injury`                             IS TRUE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 6, accident injury`                         IS NOT `work injury only`
        `the earner is insured for unemployment, under paragraph (1) of insured in section 158` IS NOT `work injury only`
        `the earner is a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`              IS `controlling`
        `the earner is an employee insured under Chapter 8, insolvency`                  IS NOT `work injury only`
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 9, disability`                              IS NOT `work injury only`
        `the earner is insured for long-term care`                                       IS NOT `work injury only`
        `the earner is a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                      IS FALSE

`v2: Avi`    MEANS `v2: an earner` "Avi" `, female:` FALSE `, born` (YMD 1985 4 1) `, paid` 15000
`v2: Amir`   MEANS `v2: an earner` "Amir" `, female:` FALSE `, born` (YMD 1985 4 1) `, paid` 10000
`v2: Galit`  MEANS `v2: an earner` "Galit" `, female:` TRUE `, born` (YMD 1988 9 15) `, paid` 20000
`v2: H3 children` MEANS LIST `v2: a child` "Dana" `, born` (YMD 2023 8 20), `v2: a child` "Eli" `, born` (YMD 2019 3 10)

