§§ `Sections 45A and 47: the pension credit`

-- N1. H1 (a single man, 10,000, March) paying 6% (600) to a pension fund, his
-- employer 12.5% (1,250), all the salary insured. Deposits 22,200 < 26,436.48:
-- not a beneficiary member, so (d): limb (2) is min(7,200, 7% x 116,400 =
-- 8,148) = 7,200 > 2,268; nothing cut: credit 35% x 7,200 = 2,520. s 47(b):
-- nothing uninsured, nil. Tax 13,435.2 - 6,534 - 2,520 = 4,381.2; a twelfth
-- 365.1; net 10,000 - 365.1 - 187.3811 - 367.5618 = 9,079.9571.
`N1 payments` MEANS `v2: paying` 600 `a month, the employer` 1250 `, insured` 10000 `, survivors' insurance` 0 `, life insurance` 0
`N1` MEANS `v2: in month` 3 `of 2026, a household of` `v2: Amir` `, married:` NOTHING `, with children` EMPTY `, health` 367.5618
#ASSERT NOT `IL-08: the earner is a beneficiary member, in` `N1` `, paying` `N1 payments`
#ASSERT `IL-07: the deduction under section 47 for the earner, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N1 payments`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `IL-07: the credit under section 45A for the earner, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N1 payments`) EQUALS 2520
#ASSERT `IL-07: the income tax for the tax year, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N1 payments`) EQUALS 4381.2
#ASSERT `IL-07: one twelfth of the income tax for the tax year, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N1 payments`) EQUALS 365.1
-- CHANGED BY THE SCHEDULE J RULING: national insurance 80.1112 + 2,297 x 7% = 240.9012
-- (was 187.3811); net 10,000 - 365.1 - 240.9012 - 367.5618 = 9,026.437 (was 9,079.9571).
#ASSERT `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N1 payments`) EQUALS 240.9012
#ASSERT `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N1 payments`) EQUALS 9026.437

-- N2. H3 (the father, 15,000, June, registered, (1A), two children) paying 6%
