-- N4. D187: N1's earner paying only 5,000 of survivors' insurance, nothing
-- insured. Limb (2) is 5,000 > 2,268, but the 1.5% proviso cuts the survivors'
-- sums to 1,746 < 2,268: by IL-08's fork F5 the floor of 2,268 then governs,
-- credit 35% x 2,268 = 793.8; IL-08 answers 35% x 1,746 = 611.1
-- (il07-tests-expected-red.l4, R3). Declined; the deduction is not affected.
-- CHANGED IN 0.3.0 (two values, were REFUSED BECAUSE "row IL-08's credit under
-- section 45A here falls below the floor of section 45A(d)(1) or (e)(1), its
-- known defect D187; IL-07 declines rather than inherit it"): row IL-08 v0.2.0
-- applies the floor after the provisos (s 45A(d), source lines 1725-1730: "לא
-- יעלה על הגבוה" of 2,268 and limb (2) as its provisos cut it, 1,746), so the
-- credit is 35% x 2,268 = 793.8, R3's figure, and the capstone passes it on.
-- Tax 13,435.2 - 6,534 - 793.8 = 6,107.4; a twelfth 508.95; net 10,000 - 508.95
-- - 240.9012 - 367.5618 = 8,882.587.
`N4 payments` MEANS `v2: paying` 0 `a month, the employer` 0 `, insured` 0 `, survivors' insurance` 5000 `, life insurance` 0
