-- from il07-tests-expected-red.l4 now that it holds (row IL-08's own answer).
#ASSERT `IL-07: the credit under section 45A for the earner, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N4 payments`) EQUALS 793.8
#ASSERT `IL-08: the credit under section 45A as row IL-08 computes it, for the earner, in` `N1` `, paying` `N4 payments` EQUALS 793.8
-- CHANGED BY THE SCHEDULE J RULING: 240.9012 (was 187.3811).
#ASSERT `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `N1` `, with further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `N4 payments`) EQUALS 240.9012

-- N5. D183: only 6,000 of life insurance: the 5% proviso (5,820) cuts sums that
-- are all at 25%. Declined in this row's words.
-- CHANGED IN 0.3.0 (was REFUSED BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not compute the credit
-- under section 45A where its limits cut sums that are all for life insurance,
-- its known defect D183; IL-07 declines"): row IL-08 v0.2.0 computes the 25%
-- class alone. s 45A(d)(2): the lower of the sums (6,000) and 7% of qualifying
-- income (8,148), within the 5% proviso for life insurance (5% x 116,400 =
-- 5,820): 5,820; the higher of it and 2,268 is 5,820; at 25% (s 45A(a)(1)):
