-- ADDED IN 0.3.0 (the second independent pass, finding F1). The Encouragement of
-- Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, s 2(a) (Sefer HaChukim
-- 3511 p. 417), exempts the income from personal exertion of an immigrant first
-- resident, or a veteran returning resident who became resident, from 5 November
-- 2025 to the end of 2026; not encoded (BACKLOG IL-36). N28: N12's woman, but
-- first immigrated on 1 December 2025. The tax and the net are declined; the
-- deduction and the allowance are not.
`N28 facts` MEANS `v2: an immigrant,` (`v2: immigrated under the Law of Return on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, the first time:` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the income tax for the tax year, in` `N12` `, with further facts` `N28 facts` BECAUSE "the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026 exempts from tax the income from personal exertion of an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident, or a veteran returning resident who became one, from 5 November 2025 to the end of tax year 2026; no composed row encodes it, and the earner's immigration falls in that period"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `N12` `, with further facts` `N28 facts` BECAUSE "the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026 exempts from tax the income from personal exertion of an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident, or a veteran returning resident who became one, from 5 November 2025 to the end of tax year 2026; no composed row encodes it, and the earner's immigration falls in that period"
-- 7,703 x 1.04% + 12,297 x 7% = 940.9012; no children.
#ASSERT `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `N12` `, with further facts` `N28 facts` EQUALS 940.9012
#ASSERT `IL-07: the child allowance for the month, in` `N12` `, with further facts` `N28 facts` EQUALS 0
-- The period's edges, and the facts that take an earner out of it: the day
-- before it begins; its first and last days; an immigration that is not the
-- first (an earlier residence, so not "לראשונה"); a returning resident with six
-- years abroad (who may have the ten of ITO s 14(a)) and with fewer (who cannot).
#ASSERT NOT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: an immigrant,` (`v2: immigrated under the Law of Return on` (YMD 2025 11 4) `, the first time:` TRUE))
#ASSERT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: an immigrant,` (`v2: immigrated under the Law of Return on` (YMD 2025 11 5) `, the first time:` TRUE))
#ASSERT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: an immigrant,` (`v2: immigrated under the Law of Return on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, the first time:` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: an immigrant,` (`v2: immigrated under the Law of Return on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, the first time:` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: further facts, paying` `v2: nothing paid`)
GIVEN `the day`    IS A DATE
      `six years`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 further facts of the household`
`v2: a returning resident, returned on` `the day` `, six years abroad:` `six years` MEANS
    `v2: an immigrant,` (`IL-07 the earner's immigration` WITH
        `the ground of immigration`                                                      IS `IL-07: a returning resident` OF `the day`, `six years`
        `the earner's Israeli citizenship was cancelled under section 10(d) of the Citizenship Law` IS FALSE
        `the day the earner became an immigrant`                                         IS `the day`
        `it was the first time the earner became an immigrant`                           IS TRUE
        `the Minister's rules under section 35(e) reach the earner`                      IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: a returning resident, returned on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `, six years abroad:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `IL-07: the earner's immigration falls in the period of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, by the further facts` (`v2: a returning resident, returned on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `, six years abroad:` FALSE)

