§§ `NII section 335, Part D, and the Schedule J switch`

-- N25. A man, 12,000, June, resident neither under the Ordinance nor under the
-- Law, not insured under Chapter 11, insured for work injury only. s 335:
-- maternity ((a): a worker not resident) and work injury; s 342(c)(1) deducts
-- maternity only: 7,703 x 0.10% + 4,297 x 0.87% = 45.0869. No credit points
-- (ss 34, 36 need residence): tax 18,192, a twelfth 1,516. Health is the
-- caller's; 0 here. Net 12,000 - 1,516 - 45.0869 = 10,438.9131. Without the
-- statuses (the 0.1.0 way in), the deduction is declined (independent finding F4).
`N25 earner` MEANS `IL-07 earner` WITH `the earner's name` IS "Ivan", `the earner is a woman` IS FALSE, `the earner's date of birth` IS YMD 1990 1 1, `the earner's monthly salary` IS 12000, `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year` IS TRUE, `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS FALSE, `the earner is a foreign worker` IS FALSE, `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE, `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE, `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE, `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE, `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS NOTHING, `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE
`N25` MEANS `v2: in month` 6 `of 2026, a household of` `N25 earner` `, married:` NOTHING `, with children` EMPTY `, health` 0
`N25 facts` MEANS `v2: with the insurance statuses` (`v2: statuses, insured for work injury only:` TRUE `, a controlling shareholder:` FALSE)
-- CHANGED BY THE SCHEDULE J RULING: at the printed totals, which are for the six
-- deduction branches together, the deduction of one who pays in maternity alone
-- cannot be told: declined (the deduction and the net; were 45.0869 and
-- 10,438.9131). At the items' reading, the alternative of the fork, 45.0869.
#ASSERT `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `N25` `, with further facts` `N25 facts` `, reading Schedule J column D as` `the sum of the items of the six deduction branches` EQUALS 45.0869
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `N25` `, with further facts` `N25 facts` BECAUSE "the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches"
#ASSERT `IL-07: the income tax for the tax year, in` `N25` `, with further facts` `N25 facts` EQUALS 18192
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `N25` `, with further facts` `N25 facts` BECAUSE "the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `N25` BECAUSE "the household does not give the earner's insurance statuses, which section 335 reads, and the earner is not resident in Israel and insured under Chapter 11"

